# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Encoding & line-ending policy for the d2r-reimagined-mod data tree.
#
# Investigation of every *.txt and *.json under data/ showed:
#   *.txt   : 100% ASCII / valid UTF-8 (no BOM), CRLF line endings.
#   *.json  : ASCII or UTF-8 (one stray UTF-8 BOM file), CRLF line endings.
#
# D2R itself loads these files at runtime; its excel/.txt and JSON parsers
# expect UTF-8 *without* a BOM and tolerate (in fact prefer) CRLF endings.
#
# This .gitattributes enforces that contract regardless of the editor or OS
# a contributor uses:
#   * `working-tree-encoding=UTF-8` -> if anyone commits a UTF-16 (or other)
#     file, Git transcodes it to UTF-8 in the stored blob; checkout always
#     materializes UTF-8 on disk.
#   * `text eol=crlf` -> the blob is normalized to LF on commit and checked
#     out as CRLF, so line endings stay stable cross-platform.
#
# After landing this file for the first time, run once to renormalize:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "chore: enforce UTF-8 + CRLF on data files"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default: let Git auto-detect text vs binary for anything not listed below.
* text=auto

# D2R excel / TSV data tables and JSON layouts/strings.
*.txt   text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8 eol=crlf
*.json  text working-tree-encoding=UTF-8 eol=crlf

# Common binary assets that must never be touched by line-ending or encoding
# conversion (belt-and-suspenders alongside .gitignore *.png).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.dds   binary
*.tga   binary
*.tbl   binary
*.dc6   binary
*.ds1   binary
*.dt1   binary
*.cof   binary
*.bin   binary
*.wav   binary
*.ogg   binary
*.mp3   binary
